<section class="wp-block-group alignfull ok-body"><!-- wp:group {"className":"ok-trows","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ok-trows"><!-- wp:group {"className":"ok-trow","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ok-trow"><!-- wp:heading {"level":3,"anchor":"front-desk","className":"ok-trow__h"} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading ok-trow__h" id="front-desk">Front Desk and Reservations</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:group {"className":"ok-trow__b","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ok-trow__b"><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ok-copy"} -->
<p class="ok-copy">Front Office training places students at the primary point of contact for guests arriving at Okami House. Under the direction of instructor Tomás Ribeiro, a former night manager who leads Term 1, students master property management software, telephone reservations, check-in protocols, and concierge inquiries. Working in groups of twelve, students manage guest folios, issue key cards, coordinate room assignments, and resolve guest requests with calm professionalism. Because Okami House operates forty-two real guest rooms, students experience the authentic pace of arrivals, departures, and billing. This department teaches precision under pressure, clear communication, and the welcoming posture required of modern hotel front office professionals.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"ok-trow","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ok-trow"><!-- wp:heading {"level":3,"anchor":"banquet-floor","className":"ok-trow__h"} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading ok-trow__h" id="banquet-floor">Banquet and Restaurant Floor</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:group {"className":"ok-trow__b","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ok-trow__b"><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ok-copy"} -->
<p class="ok-copy">The food and beverage department encompasses our sixty-cover dining room and dedicated banquet room. Led by instructor Amara Okonkwo during Term 2, students learn classical table setting, order management, wine service, and event banquet coordination. Shifts align with the student-run restaurant lunch, which welcomes the public Tuesday through Friday from 12:00 to 14:30. Students prepare dining spaces by hand, ensuring exact cutlery alignment, pristine linen presentation, and seamless floor timing between courses. From hosting intimate lunches to executing multi-course private banquets, students gain thorough familiarity with dining room choreography, guest relations, and service coordination required in first-class hospitality establishments.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"ok-trow","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ok-trow"><!-- wp:heading {"level":3,"anchor":"teaching-kitchen","className":"ok-trow__h"} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading ok-trow__h" id="teaching-kitchen">The Teaching Kitchen</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:group {"className":"ok-trow__b","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ok-trow__b"><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ok-copy"} -->
<p class="ok-copy">In the teaching kitchen, Executive Chef instructor Pieter de Wit trains students in fundamental culinary techniques, line discipline, and professional kitchen management during Term 3. Working as a cohesive brigade of twelve, students prepare fresh daily menus for the sixty-cover restaurant at Okami House. Training covers kitchen workflow, knife handling, stock preparation, temperature monitoring, and strict food safety compliance. Students learn how kitchen stations communicate with the front of house during peak service times, developing deep respect for culinary timing and portion control. This intensive kitchen experience equips hotel operations supervisors with practical knowledge essential for overseeing food and beverage operations.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"ok-trow","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ok-trow"><!-- wp:heading {"level":3,"anchor":"rooms-division","className":"ok-trow__h"} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading ok-trow__h" id="rooms-division">Rooms Division and Housekeeping</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:group {"className":"ok-trow__b","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ok-trow__b"><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ok-copy"} -->
<p class="ok-copy">Rooms Division training is led by instructor Lin Hsiao-wen during Term 3, establishing the highest housekeeping and inspection standards across Okami House. Students take full responsibility for servicing the property's forty-two guest rooms, mastering linen change routines, turn-down standards, and inventory management. Working with professional housekeeping trolleys, students learn how to turn rooms efficiently before the noon check-in deadline while maintaining impeccable hygiene and detail. Lin Hsiao-wen guides students in conducting room inspections, identifying maintenance needs, and managing laundry supply cycles. Mastering this division gives future supervisors an unshakeable foundation in the operational core that defines hotel guest satisfaction.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></section>
